  "title": "Group captivity (Hall's condition)",
  "summary": "Two batteries are each allowed both strings, and neither is individually stuck \u2014 but together they need every watt the two strings make. Deciding feasibility one sink at a time cannot see that; this is the case the max-flow solver exists for.",
  "decides": [
    "Feasibility is a property of groups of sinks, not of single sinks.",
    "A flexible sink must not take local power a tight group needs.",
    "When two captive groups contend and the configuration cannot be satisfied, which one yields."
